{{Short description|Sports teams}}
The [[2007 Rugby World Cup]] was played in France between 7 September and 20 October 2007. Each of the 20 competing nations was required to confirm their 30-man squad by 14 August. United States player [[Thretton Palamo]], aged 18 when the teams were named and 8 days past his 19th birthday when he made his only appearance in the competition, was the youngest to ever take part at a World Cup final stage.<ref>{{cite news |title=Thretton takes milestone in his stride |url=http://en.rugbyworldcup.com/home/news/newsid=2003478.html |publisher=RugbyWorldCup.com |date=6 September 2007 |access-date=7 September 2007 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20070930165324/http://en.rugbyworldcup.com/home/news/newsid%3D2003478.html |archive-date=30 September 2007 |url-status=dead }}</ref>

==Pool A==

===England===
Final squad released on 13 August 2007.<ref>[https://web.archive.org/web/20070927214522/http://www.rfu.com/index.cfm/fuseaction/RFUHome.England_Detail/StoryID/17418 RFU]</ref> [[Jamie Noon]] was sent home injured on 15 September; he was replaced by [[Newcastle Falcons]] team-mate, [[Toby Flood]].<ref>{{cite web |title=Reuters |website=[[Reuters]] |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200904044146/https://uk.reuters.com/article/uk-rugby-world-england-noon/flood-replaces-injured-noon-for-england-idUKL1714667820070917 |archive-date=2020-09-04 |url-status=dead |url=https://uk.reuters.com/article/uk-rugby-world-england-noon/flood-replaces-injured-noon-for-england-idUKL1714667820070917}}</ref> After [[Josh Lewsey]] was injured in the semi-final against [[France national rugby union team|France]], [[Nick Abendanon]] was called up as cover.<ref>{{cite web |title=England call up Abendanon for World Cup final |website=[[The Daily Telegraph]] |date=15 October 2007 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230605055853/https://www.telegraph.co.uk/sport/rugbyunion/international/england/2323411/England-call-up-Abendanon-for-World-Cup-final.html |archive-date=2023-06-05 |url-status=live |url=https://www.telegraph.co.uk/sport/rugbyunion/international/england/2323411/England-call-up-Abendanon-for-World-Cup-final.html}}</ref>

