===South Africa===
Squad released 21 July 2007<ref>[https://web.archive.org/web/20070929083023/http://www.sarugby.co.za/teams.asp?team=5222&Id=1000 SA Rugby]</ref>

[[Pierre Spies]] was withdrawn from the squad after developing a condition believed to be a [[pulmonary embolism]], with [[Bismarck du Plessis]] taking his place,<ref>{{cite news|url=https://news.bbc.co.uk/sport2/hi/rugby_union/6923349.stm |title=Springbok Spies to miss World Cup |work=[[BBC Sport]] |date=30 July 2007 |access-date=31 July 2007 }}</ref> although one specialist disputed the diagnosis.<ref>{{cite news|url=http://www.int.iol.co.za/index.php?set_id=6&click_id=3044&art_id=iol1186565645643S121 |title=Spies back in Bok picture |first=Mark |last=Keohane |newspaper=Independent Online |date=8 August 2007 |access-date=8 August 2007 }}</ref> A third specialist confirmed the original diagnosis, and Spies remained off the team.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.sarugby.co.za/default.asp?des=article&id=225336 |title=SA Rugby Statement on Pierre Spies |publisher=[[South African Rugby Union]] |date=14 August 2007 |access-date=14 August 2007 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20070926215824/http://www.sarugby.co.za/default.asp?des=article&id=225336 |archive-date=26 September 2007 |url-status=dead }}</ref>

On 10 September, after South Africa's match against [[Samoa national rugby union team|Samoa]], [[Jean de Villiers]] was ruled out of the rest of the World Cup with a torn left biceps suffered in that match. [[Wayne Julies]] replaced him on the squad.<ref name="de Villiers">{{cite web |url=http://en.rugbyworldcup.com/home/news/newsid=2006006.html |title=De Villiers out of world cup with torn bicep |publisher=International Rugby Board |date=10 September 2007 |access-date=14 September 2007 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20110715212649/http://en.rugbyworldcup.com/home/news/newsid=2006006.html |archive-date=15 July 2011 |url-status=dead }}</ref>

On 1 October, [[Jannie du Plessis]], older brother of Bismarck du Plessis, replaced [[BJ Botha]], who tore knee ligaments in South Africa's last pool match against the [[United States national rugby union team|United States]].<ref name="Jannie du Plessis">{{cite web|url=http://www.planet-rugby.com/Story/0,18259,3551_2772856,00.html |title=Planes, Trains and Bloem Babies |first=Jan |last=de Koning |website=Planet-Rugby.com |date=1 October 2007 |access-date=1 October 2007 |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20080607172644/http://www.planet-rugby.com/Story/0%2C18259%2C3551_2772856%2C00.html |archive-date=7 June 2008 }}</ref>

